  "contracts": [
    "One UserVars owner is shared by session, statement context and every production planner resolver wrapper; prepared FROM/USING, SELECT INTO and binding lookup use its live values.",
    "Bare reads select signatures from declared types, preserving source display metadata and implicit coercibility; inline assignment publishes the RHS type while planning even with zero rows or NULL values.",
    "SET plans every RHS before executing assignments and retains the physical plans; full declared type is stored with nonnull values. SET NULL removes both maps; inline NULL preserves the old value.",
    "Migration snapshots both maps under one read lock and restores them independently, without reconstructing types or discarding type-only entries.",
    "GETVAR integer signatures read the Go datum carrier, decimals use source ToDecimal without CAST scale rounding, and timestamp/duration/JSON inline assignments store strings.",
    "Go Unicode lowercase is used by live name readers/writers; original store getters/setters retain caller-supplied names as Go does."
  ],
